::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: pure-not-a-member fixture ]

==[ parser-purity ]

@rule(parser-purity){
  guard: { twrit: pure }

  pure: {
    crates: list("nope")
    forbid: list()
    allow-external: list()
  }
}

A rule naming a crate that does not exist is checking nothing, and has to
say so rather than pass.
